# Trivy deploy-gate suppressions (read automatically by the trivy-action in
# deploy.yml — "Trivy gate (CRITICAL,HIGH; fail closed)").
#
# Each entry is a DOCUMENTED, time-boxed risk-acceptance, not a "fix". Remove the
# entry as soon as the underlying dependency can be patched.
#
# ── multer 2.1.1 Denial-of-Service advisories ───────────────────────────────
# The patch is multer 2.2.0, but @nestjs/platform-express pins multer EXACTLY
# 2.1.1 (even in its latest release, 11.1.27) and npm 11.9.0 silently refuses to
# apply an `overrides` bump, so the version cannot be raised cleanly yet.
#
# Risk is mitigated and LOW in context:
#   - the only code paths that reach multer are the image-upload endpoints,
#   - which are AUTH-GATED (vendor/admin only),
#   - RATE-LIMITED (RATE_LIMIT_CALLBACK, 20/min/IP) behind Cloudflare,
#   - fileSize-capped (10 MB), and
#   - fields/parts/fieldNameSize-capped (PR #385) — which closes the
#     "deeply nested field names" DoS vector at the app layer.
#
# REMOVE these once NestJS ships a @nestjs/platform-express that depends on a
# patched multer (Dependabot will open that PR). Tracked in the project memory
# note `reference_deploy_trivy_gate`.
